{"id":"5aee7cca-e246-4b5c-a5ae-f5d206246f4c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"10476abfd15577f0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/bench/running.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f39b5c625e2b4862ca1505edd016324d829d1895","start":0,"end":38},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","register","}","from","\"","node:module","\""]},"context":{"after":"2588a330b814e437"}},"payload":{"text":"RUNNING.md, *What it costs*: what running in the debugger costs. The same programs run three ways, in Node (no\nbrowser in the way): natively on almostnode (a real run today), on tsval bare, and on tsval as the debug worker runs\nit (coverage, the profile, observed sites, the value trace). Workloads: pure computation in the program's code; data\nshuffled mostly by built-ins; a server answering requests (its handler stepped, called from almostnode's http); and a\nbuild-like run whose heavy work is in a package (native under tsval too: packages/tsval/README.md, *Modules*).\n\nnode --experimental-strip-types packages/editor/bench/running.ts [rounds]","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:04:34.064Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:04:34.064Z"}
